e given Tasks** - Only create/update/read files specified the Task sections\n- **Always quote pip version specifiers** — unquoted `>=` and `<=` are shell redirects that create empty files; use `pip install -r requirements.txt` or quote individual specifiers: `pip install \"package>=1.0\"`\n\n# Tasks\n\nUse the `Task` Tools to manage the flow of the execution.\nWhen creating the Task Definitions create it with this methodology:\n\n```\n<Agent Name>: <Task Name>\n```\n\n## Task 1: Read Related Context\n\nRead all **Input Files** listed in the prompt.\n\n## Task 2: Determine Zipsafe Status\n\nApply this decision in order — stop at the first true condition:\n\n```\nIF any CLI tools required to be bundled                                   → zip_safe: false\nELSE IF any package has C extensions (.so / .pyd)                         → zip_safe: false\nELSE IF any package accesses data files via filesystem path construction  → zip_safe: false\nELSE                                                                      → zip_safe: true  (default)\n```\n\n**Condition: \"any package accesses data files via filesystem path construction\"**\n\nThis is true when a dependency package opens a file bundled inside the zip by constructing its path from `__file__`, `__path__`, `inspect.getfile()`, or `importlib.util.find_spec().origin`. When running from inside a zip, these resolve to paths like `/path/to/extension.zip/pkg/module.py` — not real filesystem paths. Any subsequent `open()`, `os.path.isfile()`, or `os.listdir()` will fail. Packages that use `importlib.resources` instead are zip-safe (`certifi` is a correct example).\n\nTo check a package for C extensions:\n```bash\nfind $(pip show <package> | grep Location | cut -d' ' -f2)/<package> -type f \\( -name \"*.so\" -o -name \"*.pyd\" \\) | head -5\n```\n\nTo check a package for data files accessed via filesystem paths:\n```bash\nfind $(pip show <package> | grep Location | cut -d' ' -f2)/<package> -type f ! -name \"*.py\" ! -name \"*.pyc\" ! -name \"*.so\" ! -name \"*.pyd\" | head -5\n```\n\nUpdate the extension config Output File:\n- Set `zip_safe: True` or `zip_safe: False`\n\n## Task 3: Setup Dependencies\n\n**If CLI tools are needed:**\n\nCheck the analysis installation instructions for each CLI tool:\n\n- **Pre-installed on agent host (not bundled)**: Do NOT download or bundle it, skip this task.\n- **Bundled within the extension**: follow the steps below\n\nFor tools that must be downloaded:\n1. Create `vendor` if it doesn't exist\n2. Download the correct binary for the target platform specified in the analysis Input File\n3. Make binaries executable: `chmod +x`\n4. Verify the binary can be executed by running a version check\n\n**Python dependencies:**\n- Update the requirements Output File — add new packages, keep existing, sort alphabetically\n- Run: `pip install -r <requirements Output File>`\n- Run: `pip install -r requirements-dev.txt` — installs test tooling (Robot Framework, etc.) needed for the testing phase\n\n## Task 4: Document Results\n\nWrite a structured report to the documentation Output File:\n\n```markdown\n# Dependency Log\n\n## Zipsafe Decision\n- **Result**: <true|false>\n- **Reason**: <CLI tools | Packages with data files | Pure Python only>\n\n## CLI Tools\n- <binary_name>: `vendor<binary_name>` — purpose and version\n\n## Python Dependencies\n- <package>==<version> — <Pure Python | Has data files (reason)>\n\n```\n\n\n---\nWork Item ID: initial-1\nInput Files:\n- memory/initial-1/implementation-blueprint.md\nOutput Files:\n- Extension config: extension-code/src/extension.yml\n- Python requirements: extension-code/requirements.txt\n- Setup script: extension-code/setup.py\n- Dependency report: memory-ephemeral/initial-1/dependency-log.md\n"}

